<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Transfiguration Cathedral, Chernihiv</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saviour Cathedral, Chernihiv</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Transfiguration Cathedral in Chernihiv, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, is one of the oldest surviving churches of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a>. It was begun in the 1030s by Prince Mstislav of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a>, the brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-the-wise">Yaroslav the Wise</a>, who was buried there in 1036. Built of brick in the Byzantine manner with five domes, it served as the burial church of the princes of Chernigov.</p></div>
